     1	# Goal
     2	
     3	Turn the QSA HiSparse SGLang fork into an independently installed SGLang
     4	general plugin, then add exact multimodal (image) host prefix reuse, while
     5	upstreaming interfaces that shrink the plugin's internal replacements.
     6	
     7	Set 2026-10-07. Owner decisions are final unless the owner changes them.
     8	
     9	## Decisions
    10	
    11	1. Pin: SGLang `76e06febab732d28a61b75a61b7835284568cdfb`. The reference
    12	   behavior is fork `ee8fe158d64186b47236b007a299696030c372e8`. Upgrading the
    13	   pin is a separate later cycle, never mixed with migration.
    14	2. Two independent switches: `SGLANG_QSA_MODEL_COMPAT=1` (fork shared-path
    15	   behavior) and `SGLANG_QSA_HISPARSE_V3=<mode>` (offload runtime and host
    16	   prefixes; requires model compat). No switch: zero patches.
    17	3. Image prefixes are reused at every page64 boundary, including boundaries
    18	   inside an image. No outside-image-only first version.
    19	4. Upstream PRs are part of the work. Branches are prepared locally; pushing
    20	   or opening a PR waits for explicit owner confirmation each time.
    21	5. Work proceeds as parallel tasks by multiple agents. Every phase ends with a
    22	   read-only review by `gpt-6.1-sol` at `xhigh` reasoning via the Codex CLI;
    23	   findings are resolved or explicitly answered before the next phase starts.
    24	
    25	## Done means
    26	
    27	- Plugin on (`compat` and `compat+hisparse`) reproduces the fork: CPU suite,
    28	  kernel and graph checks, and frozen deterministic HTTP fixtures with equal
    29	  token IDs and exact cached bytes/state.
    30	- Plugin installed but off is pristine upstream: no patch registered, upstream
    31	  test subset passes. Non-target models are unaffected.
    32	- Any upstream edit to a patched definition fails activation (fingerprints);
    33	  activation failures stop the process (SGLang's loader swallows `Exception`).
    34	- Lease ordering is preserved: restore, async copy, logical release,
    35	  free-group flush, then physical slot reuse.
    36	- Image prefix hits match tokens, image content/preprocessing identity
    37	  (full artifact key, not the 30-bit pad value), order/offsets/grid, and
    38	  prefix M-RoPE positions, without a whole-prompt digest; page64, complete
    39	  recurrent/PLE/C4 state and the logits tail are preserved. Cold, warm and
    40	  divergent-suffix outputs are identical under the deterministic profile.
    41	- Upstream PRs for the interface and fix list in `PLAN.md` are prepared with
    42	  tests; merged ones replace the matching plugin REPLACE patches.
    43	
    44	## Constraints
    45	
    46	- Do not start, stop, or replace the production service. The owner approved
    47	  (2026-10-07) GPU validation and the interpreter
    48	  `../service/runtime-env-sglang-20260923` for it. GPU jobs run one at a time,
    49	  on ports other than production's 8081, only after checking that the GPUs
    50	  and ports are free; never kill a process the plugin work did not start.
    51	- Do not modify shared Python environments (`flash-next-env`, `quant-env`);
    52	  tests select sources with `PYTHONPATH`.
    53	- No publication (push, PR, issue, release) without explicit confirmation.
    54	- No tolerance fitting or fixture filtering; failures are reported as failures.
     1	# Parallel migration plan
     2	
     3	Goal and owner decisions: [GOAL.md](GOAL.md). This file assigns parallel
     4	tasks, file ownership, interfaces, and gates. Paths without a prefix are in
     5	this repository; `fork:` is `../qsa-hisparse` at `ee8fe158d6`; `pin:` is
     6	`../.worktrees/sglang-pin-76e06febab` (pristine SGLang `76e06febab`).
     7	
     8	## Shared rules (every agent)
     9	
    10	1. **Feature placement.** A fork change that can alter behavior while
    11	   `SGLANG_QSA_HISPARSE_V3` is unset belongs to `model_compat`; a change that
    12	   is behavior-identical to upstream whenever the HiSparse runtime is absent
    13	   belongs to `hisparse`. Record the argument in the patch's `reason`.
    14	2. **Same target in both features.** `model_compat` owns any REPLACE of a
    15	   target both features touch, copying the fork body verbatim (including its
    16	   `qsa_hisparse` branches, which are inert when the runtime is absent).
    17	   `hisparse` may add only BEFORE/AFTER/AROUND hooks on such targets.
    18	   Duplicate REPLACE fails activation.
    19	3. **REPLACE bodies are copied from the fork**, not rewritten. Allowed
    20	   mechanical edits only: explicit `super(Class, self)` for zero-argument
    21	   `super()`, plugin-owned names for custom ops/JIT modules, imports rewritten
    22	   to plugin modules, and preserved decorators (`lru_cache` etc.). List every
    23	   edit in the patch `reason` and cover it with a test. Members the fork
    24	   *added* (absent at the pin) use `attach`/`attach_value`, which fail if
    25	   upstream defines the name. Name every other upstream definition whose
    26	   behavior the copy assumes in `depends` (definitions with `@overload`
    27	   variants cannot be fingerprinted; name their callers instead).
    28	   Fingerprints: `tools/fingerprint.py write <module-name> <targets...>`,
    29	   always against `pin:`. Never hand-edit hashes.
    30	4. **Prefer the narrowest hook.** AFTER/AROUND at a function boundary first;
    31	   REPLACE only for mid-function insertion. Each REPLACE is listed in
    32	   `docs/patch-inventory.md` with the upstream interface that would remove it.
