   177	## 3. Non-Python changes: a plugin-owned Marlin MoE JIT copy
   178	
   179	Files: `kernels/jit/csrc/gemm/marlin_moe/{marlin_template.h, moe_wna16_marlin.cuh}`
   180	(modified) and `stripe_schedule.h` (new), plus `kernels/ops/moe/moe_wna16_marlin.py`.
   181	With `kDeterministicReduce = false` (the template default, gated by
   182	`if constexpr`) the fork's kernel is source-equivalent to upstream. The plugin
   183	therefore needs its copy only for J03, and the in-tree op is left unpatched.
   184	
   185	**Confirmed feasible** at the pin:
   186	
   187	- `load_jit(*args, cuda_files=..., cuda_wrappers=..., extra_include_paths=..., ...)`
   188	  is at `kernels/jit/utils/compile/loader.py:48`. `resolve_sources`
   189	  (`spec.py:125-134`) passes absolute paths through unchanged; relative paths
   190	  resolve against the in-tree `csrc/`. With `header_only=True` (the default)
   191	  the generated `cuda.cu` does `#include "<absolute path>"` and exports each
   192	  wrapper with `TVM_FFI_DLL_EXPORT_TYPED_FUNC` inside `namespace sglang`
   193	  (`spec.py:111-122`).
   194	- Include flags are plain `-I` in this order: toolchain base, then
   195	  `DEFAULT_INCLUDE = [KERNEL_PATH/include]` (`paths.py:30`), then
   196	  `extra_include_paths` (`loader.py:89`, `ninja.py:83-84`). Quoted includes
   197	  search the including file's directory first, then the `-I` list.
   198	- The plugin copy lives at `kernels/csrc/marlin_moe/` and holds all four files:
   199	  the fork's `moe_wna16_marlin.cuh`, `marlin_template.h` and
   200	  `stripe_schedule.h`, plus `kernel.h`, which is unchanged but copied so that
   201	  no `marlin_moe` sibling can resolve to the in-tree copy. It is shipped by the
   202	  existing `kernels/csrc/**/*` package-data rule.
   203	- The fork headers include `"../marlin/{dequant.h,marlin.cuh,marlin_dtypes.cuh}"`,
   204	  and `kernel.h` includes `"../marlin/..."`. Pass
   205	  `extra_include_paths=[str(KERNEL_PATH / "csrc" / "gemm" / "marlin")]` so that
   206	  `../marlin/x` resolves to the installed in-tree `csrc/gemm/marlin/x`. Those
   207	  headers include only siblings and `<sgl_kernel/...>` (from `DEFAULT_INCLUDE`).
   208	  Do not use `.../gemm/marlin_moe` as the include path: a header the plugin
   209	  forgot to copy would then silently resolve to the unmodified in-tree file.
   210	  With `.../gemm/marlin` a missing `kernel.h` resolves to the dense-Marlin
   211	  `kernel.h` and fails to compile loudly instead.
   212	- Cache identity. `module_name = "sgl_kernel_jit_" + "_".join(args)`
   213	  (`spec.py:20,55-57`). The cache directory is
   214	  `<SGLANG_JIT_CACHE_DIR>/<target>/<module_name>/build-<build_key>/deps-<deps_key>/`
   215	  (`cache.py:306`). `build_key` hashes `module_args`, the direct source
   216	  contents, the generated ninja text and the environment (`cache.py:259-289`).
   217	  `deps_key` hashes the transitive includes, so an edit to the in-tree
   218	  `../marlin` headers rebuilds the plugin module. Pruning is scoped per
   219	  build-key directory (`cache.py:441-466`).
   220	- **Args that avoid collisions**: use a distinct marker as the first
   221	  positional arg and append the fourth template arg:
   222	  `load_jit("qsa_hisparse_moe_wna16_marlin", *make_cpp_args(dtype, is_ep, has_bias, use_deterministic_reduce), cuda_files=[str(PLUGIN_CSRC / "marlin_moe/moe_wna16_marlin.cuh")], cuda_wrappers=[("qsa_moe_wna16_marlin_gemm", f"moe_wna16_marlin_gemm<{args}>")], extra_include_paths=[...])`.
   223	  The module name becomes
   224	  `sgl_kernel_jit_qsa_hisparse_moe_wna16_marlin_<dtype>_<ep>_<bias>_<det>`,
   225	  which differs from the in-tree `sgl_kernel_jit_moe_wna16_marlin_<dtype>_<ep>_<bias>`.
   226	  The `.so` basename and cache directory are therefore distinct. A distinct
   227	  export name (`qsa_moe_wna16_marlin_gemm`) also avoids two loaded libraries
   228	  exporting the same `extern "C"` `__tvm_ffi_*` symbol. `build_key` would
   229	  differ even with the same marker, but the shared `<module_name>` directory
   230	  and `.so` basename are avoidable.
   231	- Residual risk: both libraries define C++ entities in
   232	  `sglang::device::marlin_moe`. Every template the fork changed gained the
   233	  extra `bool` parameter, so its mangled names differ. The remaining
   234	  non-template inline code is identical, so symbol interposition would be
   235	  harmless. W5 should still confirm how `tvm_ffi.load_module` calls `dlopen`
   236	  (`RTLD_LOCAL` avoids interposition entirely). `SGLANG_CRASH_ON_JIT_COMPILE`
   237	  (`loader.py:131`) also applies to the plugin module: GPU windows that set
   238	  it need the cache seeded.
   239	
   240	## 4. Hidden shared-path changes (behavior changes with HiSparse unset)
   241	
   242	Status: **confirmed** (as described), **corrected**, or **new** (not in the
   243	known list).
   244	
   245	1. **Confirmed (M04).** `ReqToTokenPool.clear` no longer zeroes
   246	   `req_generation`. Readers: `managers/overlap_utils.py:212,232`
   247	   (stale-result generation ring) and `speculative/dspark_components/dspark_planner.py:349,398`.
   248	   The disaggregated `DecodeReqToTokenPool.clear` (`disaggregation/decode.py:230`)
   249	   still zeroes its own copy, which the fork leaves inconsistent.
   250	2. **Confirmed, and stronger (F01).** The new `ForwardBatch` fields are not
   251	   just passive. `req_pool_indices_cpu` is non-None for scheduled batches, and
   252	   `kv_allocated_lens_cpu` is non-None whenever `seq_lens_cpu` is None.
   253	   `TboForwardBatchPreparer.filter_batch` raises for any non-None field it does
   254	   not handle (`batch_overlap/two_batch_overlap.py:845-851`), so with the fork
   255	   two-batch overlap fails for every model. `kv_allocated_lens_cpu` has no
   256	   reader anywhere in the fork, and it adds a per-batch Python list build.
   257	3. **Corrected (G01).** Moving `shape_key` out of `canary_ctx` is
   258	   behavior-identical. `_make_graph_key` builds a `ShapeKey` from its arguments,
   259	   and `_capture_graph_size` reads `self.ragged_verify_mode`, set at
   260	   construction. Every subclass that overrides `_make_graph_key` (EAGLE draft,
   261	   draft-extend, multi-layer EAGLE, frozen-KV MTP) also overrides
   262	   `capture_one_shape`. XPU and NPU inherit both. G01 is therefore hisparse.
   263	4. **Confirmed, with detail (Q04, Q10, Q12, A01-A09).** QSA FP8 descale:
   264	   - `_store_kv` passes k/v scales and cloned K/V to `set_kv_buffer` for FP8
   265	     caches with non-unit `k_scale_float`/`v_scale_float`.
   266	   - Decode and trtllm extraction dequantize with those scales.
   267	   - The FP8 path of the prefill Triton kernels changes accumulation order
   268	     (`acc*alpha + dot*v_scale`) even with unit scales: callers pass no scales.
   269	   - New `ValueError`s: K/V dtype mismatch, queries not BF16/FP16, non-FP8 K/V
   270	     dtype different from Q.
   271	   - The decode scratch dtype becomes `k_buffer.dtype` for non-FP8 KV
   272	     (previously `q.dtype`). This is identical when the dtypes match.
   273	5. **Confirmed (Q01).** The SM86/SM89 fallback applies only when FA2
   274	   `flash_attn` is not importable. It selects SGLang's vendored
   275	   `flash_attn_varlen_func` instead of FA4 cute. Separately, the SM89 FlashInfer
   276	   ragged FA2 path (Q07, Q09) is hisparse-only. PLAN's "SM89 fallback" covers
   277	   both SM86 and SM89 for the first.
   278	6. **Confirmed (Q05, T04).** `decode_score_width` changes only eager plain
   279	   decode, without spec decoding or MTP reuse: the MQA score stride becomes
   280	   `ceil(ceil(context_len/ratio)/page)*page`, matching the graph, instead of the
   281	   batch's page-table width. Graph decode is unchanged.
   282	7. **Confirmed, plus new items (Z01, Z02).** In `create_weights`, the w2 group
   283	   scales are sized without `moe_tp_size` and the scales are `params_dtype`
   284	   instead of fp16. **New:** in `process_weights_after_loading`, the w13
   285	   `marlin_moe_permute_scales(size_k=...)` now derives K from the scale tensor
   286	   instead of `intermediate_size_per_partition`, and each repack is followed by
   287	   `gc.collect()` and `torch.cuda.empty_cache()`. This changes load-time peak
   288	   memory for every GPTQ Marlin MoE model.
   289	8. **Confirmed (Z03, Z04).** For AutoRound g128 MoE layers that Marlin rejects
   290	   (TP2, K=320), the fork switches to Marlin g64 and expands each scale and
   291	   qzero row twice at load. Upstream would use the non-Marlin MoE path.
   292	9. **Confirmed, plus new items (E03, E06, E07, E08).** INT8-row PLE. **New:**
   293	   `Qwen4ExpNGramEmbedding` now builds its table on the `meta` device for
   294	   *every* `ple_offload_embedding` config, including bf16 and fp8 (a
   295	   memory-peak change). `load_weights` adds hard errors for int8 storage
   296	   mismatches and NaN row-scale coverage.
   297	10. **Confirmed (U01), plus a new item (Z05).** Log level: `freeze_gc` changes
   298	    from debug to info. **New:** `FusedMoE.__init__`'s deferred-finalize log
   299	    also changes from debug to info.
   300	11. **Confirmed (S03).** `multimodal_inputs` is set on the HiSparse decode
   301	    batch. This affects only upstream `--enable-hisparse` with multimodal
   302	    requests.
   303	12. **New (J01-J04).** Deterministic Marlin MoE: with
   304	    `enable_deterministic_inference`, every Marlin MoE model uses stable token
   305	    alignment, `block_size_m = 8`, no atomic add, and the whole-K reduce.
   306	13. **New (T01-T03).** Deterministic QSA top-k: with deterministic inference,
   307	    selection is the stable top-k and decode skips the JIT `fast_topk`.
   308	14. **New (H03-H08, E01-E02).** Stable HC: with deterministic inference,
   309	    Qwen4Exp's `GatedResidual.mix` uses the stable fused kernel when it is
   310	    supported. Previously the fused path was disabled and the torch.compile
   311	    chain ran.
   312	15. **New, negligible (Q12).** NVTX ranges in `_forward_paged_attention` are
   313	    emitted only when operations NVTX profiling is enabled.
