   177	## 3. Non-Python changes: a plugin-owned Marlin MoE JIT copy
   178	
   179	Files: `kernels/jit/csrc/gemm/marlin_moe/{marlin_template.h, moe_wna16_marlin.cuh}`
   180	(modified) and `stripe_schedule.h` (new), plus `kernels/ops/moe/moe_wna16_marlin.py`.
   181	With `kDeterministicReduce = false` (the template default, gated by
   182	`if constexpr`) the fork's kernel is source-equivalent to upstream. The plugin
   183	therefore needs its copy only for J03, and the in-tree op is left unpatched.
   184	
   185	**Confirmed feasible** at the pin:
   186	
   187	- `load_jit(*args, cuda_files=..., cuda_wrappers=..., extra_include_paths=..., ...)`
   188	  is at `kernels/jit/utils/compile/loader.py:48`. `resolve_sources`
   189	  (`spec.py:125-134`) passes absolute paths through unchanged; relative paths
   190	  resolve against the in-tree `csrc/`. With `header_only=True` (the default)
   191	  the generated `cuda.cu` does `#include "<absolute path>"` and exports each
   192	  wrapper with `TVM_FFI_DLL_EXPORT_TYPED_FUNC` inside `namespace sglang`
   193	  (`spec.py:111-122`).
   194	- Include flags are plain `-I` in this order: toolchain base, then
   195	  `DEFAULT_INCLUDE = [KERNEL_PATH/include]` (`paths.py:30`), then
   196	  `extra_include_paths` (`loader.py:89`, `ninja.py:83-84`). Quoted includes
   197	  search the including file's directory first, then the `-I` list.
   198	- The plugin copy lives at `kernels/csrc/marlin_moe/` and holds all four files:
   199	  the fork's `moe_wna16_marlin.cuh`, `marlin_template.h` and
   200	  `stripe_schedule.h`, plus `kernel.h`, which is unchanged but copied so that
   201	  no `marlin_moe` sibling can resolve to the in-tree copy. It is shipped by the
   202	  existing `kernels/csrc/**/*` package-data rule.
   203	- The fork headers include `"../marlin/{dequant.h,marlin.cuh,marlin_dtypes.cuh}"`,
   204	  and `kernel.h` includes `"../marlin/..."`. Pass
   205	  `extra_include_paths=[str(KERNEL_PATH / "csrc" / "gemm" / "marlin")]` so that
   206	  `../marlin/x` resolves to the installed in-tree `csrc/gemm/marlin/x`. Those
   207	  headers include only siblings and `<sgl_kernel/...>` (from `DEFAULT_INCLUDE`).
   208	  Do not use `.../gemm/marlin_moe` as the include path: a header the plugin
   209	  forgot to copy would then silently resolve to the unmodified in-tree file.
   210	  With `.../gemm/marlin` a missing `kernel.h` resolves to the dense-Marlin
   211	  `kernel.h` and fails to compile loudly instead.
   212	- Cache identity. `module_name = "sgl_kernel_jit_" + "_".join(args)`
   213	  (`spec.py:20,55-57`). The cache directory is
   214	  `<SGLANG_JIT_CACHE_DIR>/<target>/<module_name>/build-<build_key>/deps-<deps_key>/`
   215	  (`cache.py:306`). `build_key` hashes `module_args`, the direct source
   216	  contents, the generated ninja text and the environment (`cache.py:259-289`).
   217	  `deps_key` hashes the transitive includes, so an edit to the in-tree
   218	  `../marlin` headers rebuilds the plugin module. Pruning is scoped per
   219	  build-key directory (`cache.py:441-466`).
   220	- **Args that avoid collisions**: use a distinct marker as the first
   221	  positional arg and append the fourth template arg:
   222	  `load_jit("qsa_hisparse_moe_wna16_marlin", *make_cpp_args(dtype, is_ep, has_bias, use_deterministic_reduce), cuda_files=[str(PLUGIN_CSRC / "marlin_moe/moe_wna16_marlin.cuh")], cuda_wrappers=[("qsa_moe_wna16_marlin_gemm", f"moe_wna16_marlin_gemm<{args}>")], extra_include_paths=[...])`.
   223	  The module name becomes
   224	  `sgl_kernel_jit_qsa_hisparse_moe_wna16_marlin_<dtype>_<ep>_<bias>_<det>`,
   225	  which differs from the in-tree `sgl_kernel_jit_moe_wna16_marlin_<dtype>_<ep>_<bias>`.

